For `writeOkWith()` you need to not flush when sending the EOF variation of the OK packet.

And in `writeColumnInfo()` you should neither send EOF or OK packets.

This looks more how MySQL 8.0 behaves as checked with Wireshark and for me results in a working MySQL Client connection.

```patch
diff --git a/server/conn.go b/server/conn.go
index 39a088fbd..c44c858f6 100644
--- a/server/conn.go
+++ b/server/conn.go
@@ -1469,6 +1469,9 @@ func (cc *clientConn) writeOkWith(ctx context.Context, header byte, msg string,
                return err
        }
 
+       if header == mysql.EOFHeader {
+               return nil
+       }
        return cc.flush(ctx)
 }
 
@@ -2141,6 +2144,9 @@ func (cc *clientConn) writeColumnInfo(ctx context.Context, columns []*ColumnInfo
                        return err
                }
        }
+       if cc.capability&mysql.ClientDeprecateEof > 0 {
+               return nil
+       }
        return cc.writeEOF(ctx, serverStatus)
 }
 
```
